The plate is a square, roughly 26 cm across, and the food covers only a small part of it. There is a portion of roasted or braised pork, perhaps 2-3 slices, with some onion or carrot on top. Next to it is a small pile of cooked greens, probably chard, with beet pieces.

I estimate the pork at about 120 g. Cooked pork shoulder runs about 220 kcal per 100 g, so that is roughly 260 kcal. The greens and beets are about 80 g, and with some oil that comes to around 60 kcal. Together that is about 200 g of food and about 320 kcal.

